Z||000004||FieroLisa||07-26-2001||10:05 PM||||I remember the day that accident happened- cause a couple of people thought it had been me in the Fiero.... that crash happened about 3 minutes from my old house. <P>Also remember stopping by the police station after someone hit me and ran, ya know, to report it, and seeing a whole bunch of pics of that Fiero- really messed up!!!!<P>And yet another funny thing, the Anthony Peppeard who was quoted in that article was related to one of my ex boyfriends.<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000005||California Kid||07-26-2001||10:21 PM||||Don't mean to sound cold, but the damage to that Fiero doesn't look too bad considering the circumstances. Just shows how well these cars are constructed. Most other cars would have had their roofs sheared off.<P>Who know's if she was wearing her seat belt, article doesn't doesn't state??? At least the kid or kids still have a father !!!<P>FYI, I've read a couple articles that the Fiero is the safest vehicle GM has ever developed when it comes to collision. Don't know if it's true, but I've seen quite a few accident reports on Fiero's where you really wonder how anyone got out alive. There was an article over the last year or two about one lady who got hit by a train, was dragged 4-5 miles, and used her cell phone to call 911 (while she's being dragged), yelling her location and to stop the train !!! She was cut out of the car with only cuts and bruises.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Steve Normington||07-27-2001||12:22 AM||||I think everyone has missed an important point.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>William and Rhonda dropped their 4-year-old off at the babysitters.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What the bleep were they doing with a 4-year old and two adults in a Fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ferrari_cdn||07-27-2001||12:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>My god man! A young wife and mother died and all you can say is ( It's sad seeing a Fiero wrecked. My prayers go out to that young woman and her family.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Of course, I have my prayers for them.  I'm sorry it was misleading.  I admit that I have a tendency to not think before typing.||||reg||1
