Z||000009||87GTBro||07-27-2001||12:54 AM||||That is heartbreaking...  Can you imagine being the husband?  I don't want to think about it...<P>It bugs me that people driving trucks don't pay attention to small cars.  I'm not just talking about semi drivers either.  There is an increasing number of people driving full size pickups with 8" lifts and 35 series tires.  Isn't there a law about how far your bumper has to be from the ground?  If I was rear-ended by one of these trucks or rear-ended one of them, I would be decapitated!  It scares me.<P>Just today, a truck started creeping into my lane on the highway as I was passing him.  Like it's really all that difficult to see me coming.  I was right beside him when he did it too.  He didn't see me until my nose inched out passed him in the front a little, then he swerved back into his lane so hard he almost lost control.<P>Some people's kids.  Sorry for venting on you.  Here's a rag to wipe off the sweat...<P>------------------<BR>AOL IM: GTFiero86Dan<BR>'86 GT 4 speed<BR>'87 GT Auto<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GTBrosig1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||DecadenceR||07-27-2001||01:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B>FYI, I've read a couple articles that the Fiero is the safest vehicle GM has ever developed when it comes to collision. Don't know if it's true, but I've seen quite a few accident reports on Fiero's where you really wonder how anyone got out alive.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I wrecked a Fiero once. 87 coupe. When it got towed to my house, it didnt' look too bad t all. But somehow the front end was totally wrecked. The spare tire was totally vertical and the whole under hood area was pushed back into it. Funny thing is, i didn't move out of my seat a bit (wasn't wearing a seatbelt) and my CD player didn't even skip.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||07-27-2001||09:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B>I think everyone has missed an important point.<P> What the bleep were they doing with a 4-year old and two adults in a Fiero?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I wondered the same thing, myself.<BR>In GA, somebody would have possibly gone to jail for that.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
